course: dictionary
lesson: 6895
title: Overuse: too much of a good thing
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: Overuse is made of two parts: over, meaning too much, and use. As a verb, it means to use something too much or too often. «Bacteria can become resistant to antibiotics if the medicines are overused.» The medicines are used too often, so they stop working well.
explain: As a noun, overuse means using something so much that it gets wasted, worn out, harmful or boring. «Far too much of the same exercise every day leads to overuse pain.» Here the body is hurt by too much of one thing, even a healthy thing like exercise.
explain: In English, overusing a word like «nice» or «said» makes your writing dull. Good writers pick different words. When a phrase is used so often that it sounds stale, it is called a cliché.
fact: Overuse means using something too much or too often.
fact: As a verb, the forms are overuse, overuses, overused and overusing. As a noun, overuse is uncountable.
fact: «Overuse injuries» happen in sport when the same movement is repeated too often without enough rest.
fact: A «cliché» is a phrase that is overused, so it has become dull.
fact: Rest is part of training: take at least one or two days a week off your main sport.
exercise: «Bacteria can become resistant to antibiotics if the medicines are overused.» What does overused mean here? | Put away on a high shelf | Made stronger and bigger | Used carefully and only when really needed | *Used too much or too often
exercise: Why do doctors not give antibiotics for colds? | Because colds go away faster without them | Because antibiotics taste bad to children | Because colds are too strong for medicine | *Because overusing them can make bacteria resistant
exercise: In «Playing too long without breaks can cause overuse injuries», what causes the injuries? | Warm-up stretches | Playing with friends | *Playing too long without breaks | Drinking plenty of water
test: Your story says «nice» on every page. What is the problem? | It is too short to read | It shows you have a huge vocabulary | *It is overused, so the writing becomes dull | It is a verb, so it cannot describe things
test: Which sentence uses overuse as a noun? | Drink a glass of water every day | The water was cold and clear | *Overuse of water can harm the land | Water is used to wash the car
exam: Which best describes an overuse injury? | A sore throat from shouting at a match | A cut from falling off a bike | *Pain caused by doing the same sport too often without a rest | A bruise from being hit by a ball
